-- Beast Lore says "Cannot Be Tamed" on tameable beasts (Mangy Wolf 525, foxes, bears, wolves: Tasko, 0.1.34).
-- Blizzard's live WoW Forever realm answers the creature query of these beasts with type flags 0x08000001 (tameable plus bit
-- 0x08000000), and of the other beasts with 0x08000000. Ours answers 0x00000001 / 0x00000000: bit 0x08000000 is missing (player
-- cache recorded on our realm, cache-1109b). Live sets that bit on 97% of classic creatures (2190 of 2248 entries below 200000 in
-- the live caches). The server code does not use it (TC calls it CREATURE_TYPE_FLAG_FORCE_GOSSIP); it is the only difference
-- in the flags the client gets, so the Forever client's Beast Lore line is taken to read it. Not checked in a client here.
-- Source: live player caches enUS/deDE/ruRU, builds 70790/70862 (cache-1108b), every beast (creature type 1) in them:
-- 211 tameable beasts with 0x08000001, 108 other beasts with 0x08000000. Beasts only; the bits are OR-ed in,
-- nothing else changes. Clients keep creature data in Cache\WDB: delete that folder before checking in game. Safe to run again.
